      <!-- Quality assurance -->
      <Section
        id="quality-assurance"
        index="06"
        eyebrow="Assurance"
        title="Quality assurance and learning"
        lead="A reporting service is only as defensible as the system that checks it. Assurance is a matter of record, not of intention."
      >
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="entry">
            <h3 class="entry-title">Peer review and discrepancy audit</h3>
            <p class="para-sm pl-3">A documented sample of reports is re-read by another competent reporter; discrepancies are classified, discussed and the learning recorded. The RCR recommends regular discrepancy meetings and a blame-free learning culture. Done properly, the audit trail is also the evidence that the service was monitoring its own accuracy.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="entry">
            <h3 class="entry-title">Candour and correction</h3>
            <p class="para-sm pl-3">Where a report is wrong or a study misread, the professional duty of candour runs in parallel with the incident process: acknowledge, explain, apologise, record and share the learning. An addendum supplements the original report; it does not replace it. The statutory duty of candour binds organisations and is triggered by moderate harm or above; the professional duty binds the individual clinician.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="entry">
            <h3 class="entry-title">Audit of unreported studies</h3>
            <p class="para-sm pl-3">Unreported investigations should be audited at a defined interval, commonly annually. This is a service-level assurance activity, distinct from individual discrepancy review, and evidences that the reporting backlog is monitored and escalated rather than merely accumulating.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="entry">
            <h3 class="entry-title">Keep the record, not just the report</h3>
            <p class="para-sm pl-3">Protocol detail, the clinical information supplied, viewing conditions, the route by which an urgent finding was communicated and any escalation attempt are often the decisive material years later. A contemporaneous note of an escalation attempt carries more weight than a later recollection.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Section>
